d3d12core: enable VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace, so HDR swapchains get HDR surface formats.

vkd3d-proton never asked the instance for VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace. On drivers that list HDR color spaces only
when it is enabled (KosmicKrisp, Mesa's common WSI), the surface offered sRGB alone, SetColorSpace1 of
DXGI_COLOR_SPACE_RGB_FULL_G2084_NONE_P2020 (HDR10) or G10_NONE_P709 (scRGB) failed with E_INVALIDARG, and a game that
went on rendering HDR wrote PQ values into an sRGB swapchain: a washed-out grey picture. The extension is optional, so
nothing changes where it is missing; an unsupported color space is now logged.

It reaches every game with an FP16 swapchain, not only HDR ones: DXVK's dxgi puts every R16G16B16A16_FLOAT swapchain
in scRGB whenever the presenter accepts that color space, which it now does on KosmicKrisp. What the display does with
scRGB is up to the driver (KosmicKrisp 0011 gives it default HDR metadata only when asked). HDR10 still needs
DXVK_HDR=1: DXVK only accepts the HDR10 color space with enableHDR set. It changes the MoltenVK route as well, which
was not tried with Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 (we do not have it).

Checked on an M5 Max, macOS 27.2, KosmicKrisp (2026-11-17): Forza Horizon 6 sets color space 12 (HDR10) and EA SPORTS
FC 27 color space 1 (scRGB), both accepted, both shown as HDR. Builds with the renderers' llvm-mingw for x86-64 on top
of 0001 to 0012.

Upstream: not sent.

diff --git a/libs/d3d12core/main.c b/libs/d3d12core/main.c
index a8498bca..4ebcdfe7 100644
--- a/libs/d3d12core/main.c
+++ b/libs/d3d12core/main.c
@@ -581,6 +581,8 @@ static HRESULT vkd3d_create_instance_global(struct vkd3d_instance **out_instance
         VK_KHR_SURFACE_MAINTENANCE_1_EXTENSION_NAME,
         VK_EXT_SURFACE_MAINTENANCE_1_EXTENSION_NAME,
         VK_KHR_GET_SURFACE_CAPABILITIES_2_EXTENSION_NAME,
+        /* HDR10 and scRGB surface formats for SetColorSpace1 */
+        VK_EXT_SWAPCHAIN_COLOR_SPACE_EXTENSION_NAME,
 #ifndef _WIN32
         /* TODO: We need to attempt to dlopen() native DXVK DXGI and handle this more gracefully. */
         "VK_KHR_xcb_surface",
diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
index 8dd2cc10..9bb0c786 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/swapchain.c
@@ -1278,7 +1278,10 @@ static HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE dxgi_vk_swap_chain_SetColorSpace(IDXGIVkSwapCha
     struct dxgi_vk_swap_chain *chain = impl_from_IDXGIVkSwapChain(iface);
     TRACE("iface %p, ColorSpace %u.\n", iface, ColorSpace);
     if (!dxgi_vk_swap_chain_supports_color_space(chain, ColorSpace))
+    {
+        WARN("Color space %#x is not supported by the surface.\n", ColorSpace);
         return E_INVALIDARG;
+    }
 
     chain->user.dxgi_color_space_type = ColorSpace;
     chain->user.modifies_hdr_metadata = true;
